ary for photosynthesis"],"resources":["Relevant equipment and apparatus, heat sources, water, relevant chemicals and reagents, leaves, pond weeds, nutrition-in-plants models/charts, and online resources","Periods shared with 'Introduction to Biology' and 'Cell Structure and Organization' (27, under 1.1) and with 'Scientific Process' (40, under 3.1)"],"assessment":[],"periods":"27 (shared) + 40 (shared)"}],[{"topic":"Nutrition in Mammals","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, principles and processes of Biology / 2.0 Conduct biological investigations","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Describe the physiological, anatomical and ecological processes of living organisms / 2.1 Demonstrate mastery of basic skills for conducting biological investigations","activities":["Describe nutrition in human and ruminants (nutrients, digestive system and processes)","Investigate food nutrients in various food samples"],"methods":["Brainstorming: concept of nutrition in human and ruminants","Jigsaw: nutrients, nutritional deficiency and disorders","ICT-Based learning: digestive system and digestion processes through simulation","Group discussion: diseases and disorders of the human digestive system","Laboratory practical: investigate food nutrients in various food samples"],"resources":["Variety of food substances, charts/pictures of food nutrients, models/charts of human and ruminant digestive systems, dissected mammal specimen, charts/photographs of common disorders and diseases of the digestive system, relevant reagents/chemicals and apparatus"],"assessment":[],"periods":"64 (shared) + 31 (shared)"},{"topic":"Digestive System","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, principles and processes of Biology","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Describe the physiological, anatomical and ecological processes of living organisms","activities":["Describe nutrition in human and ruminants — digestive system component (nutrients, digestive system and processes)"],"methods":["ICT-Based