 capital for small businesses are clearly described"],"periods":"34 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"Microfinancing and Cooperatives in Business Formation and Operations","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of business knowledge","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, theories and principles of Business Education","activities":["Describe the role of microfinancing and cooperatives in facilitating business formation and operations"],"methods":["Brainstorming to identify financial institutions that give small loans (microcredits) to small business owners","Scenarios portraying the role of microfinances and cooperatives, followed by summarising lessons learned","Linking the scenarios to microfinances and cooperatives available in the community"],"resources":["Online/offline sources"],"assessment":["The role of microfinancing and cooperatives in facilitating business formation and operations is clearly described"],"periods":"34 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"Management of Small Businesses (Records, Profit and Loss, Budgeting)","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Describe the basic aspects of management for small businesses (meaning, financial and other records keeping, calculation of profit and loss, budgeting, and control and administration)"],"methods":["Brainstorming on the roles of a head of school, head of a family, business owner, club leader and head prefect, linked to the meaning and functions of management","Think-ink-pair-share on sources and uses of income for an individual or family, assessing income against expenses to explain the meaning of a budget","Project activity: prepare a monthly cash budget for the business club using a budget template"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and a budget template"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of management for small businesses are described"],"periods":"26 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Warehousing and Inventorying for Small Businesses","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Describe the basic aspects of warehousing and inventorying (including the documents used)"],"methods":["Group activity analysing goods sold in a manufacturing or trading business and identifying the documents the business club would use"],"resources":["Online/offline sources; samples of goods received note, goods release note and bin card"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of warehousing and inventorying for small businesses are described"],"periods":"26 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Identifying Business Opportunities in the Local Environment","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Apply business knowledge in various contexts","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Apply business theories into practice","activities":["Identify business opportunities available in the local environment"],"methods":["Brainstorming by economic sector to identify business ideas that suit the local area","Gallery walk where groups add missing ideas to other groups' sheets, then agree on the most applicable ideas","Group discussion and presentation of an identified opportunity","Skills lab: prepare and present a business pitch guide (business idea and goals, problem, solution, target market, marketing strategy, industry analysis, management team, competition, current status, amount requested, projected use of funds), with feedback from a pitch rubric","Project activity: polish and rehearse the pitch, then pitch to the business club or a panel of investors"],"resources":["Online/offline sources, tools, pitch guide template and pitch rubric"],"assessment":["The business opportunities available in the local environment are identified"],"periods":"10 (Specific Competence 3.1)"}],[{"topic":"Marketing for Small Businesses","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of business knowledge","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, theories and principles of Business Education","activities":["Describe the basic aspects of marketing for small businesses (meaning and importance, product, price, place/distribution, promotion)"],"methods":["Group activity identifying business activities in the community or business club and how owners influence customers","Case study on the marketing activities of an operating small business in the community"],"resources":["Online/offline sources"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of marketing for small businesses are clearly explained"],"periods":"42 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"E-marketing for Small Businesses","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of business knowledge","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, theories and principles of Business Education","activities":["Describe the basic aspects of e-marketing for small businesses (including uploading a business biography in social media)"],"methods":["Scenario portraying the meaning and importance of e-marketing, with a summary of lessons learned","Group activity discussing the features of e-marketing that enable small businesses to operate effectively, followed by presentations"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and a business biography template"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of e-marketing for small businesses are clearly described"],"periods":"42 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"Policy and Regulatory Environment Governing Small Businesses in Tanzania","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Explore the basic aspects of the policy and regulatory environment governing small businesses in Tanzania (roles of government and non-governmental agencies, policies, laws and by-laws)"],"methods":["Group activity discussing school rules and regulations controlling club activities, linked to regulations governing small business operations","Case study of a business that does not pay taxes and levies and sells illegal products, analysing the consequences of non-compliance and how to comply in the business club"],"resources":["Online/offline sources"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of the policy and regulatory environment governing small businesses in Tanzania are appropriately explored"],"periods":"52 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Registering Small Businesses in Tanzania","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Describe procedures for registering small businesses in Tanzania (types of licences, importance of registration, and sanctions for non-compliance)"],"methods":["Reflection on the importance of business compliance and certification, linked to types of licences and the importance of registration","Field trip to nearby businesses to find out their licences, why they registered and the consequences of non-compliance"],"resources":["Online/offline sources, registration guide and licence template"],"assessment":["The procedures for registering small businesses in Tanzania are clearly described"],"periods":"52 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Developing a Business Plan","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Apply business knowledge in various contexts","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Apply business theories into practice","activities":["Develop a plan for a small business identified from the opportunities in Form II (identification, financing, production and distribution, and marketing)"],"methods":["Brainstorming on the meaning and importance of business planning","Case study of a small business plan from the community or business club covering business description, operating activities, market analysis and marketing plan"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and a business plan template"],"assessment":["A plan for a small business identified from the business opportunities in Form Two is appropriately developed"],"periods":"28 (Specific Competence 3.1)"},{"topic":"Basic Tenets of Ethics for Small Businesses","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Apply business knowledge in various contexts","scCode":"3.2","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic business ethics","activities":["Describe the basic tenets of ethics for small businesses (meaning, norms and values)"],"methods":["Brainstorming on norms and values in the community, linked to the meaning and importance of ethics in operating businesses in Tanzania","Skills lab: write personal values that influence business operations, explain how to promote them in the business club, and develop ethics guides for the businesses","Project activity: a report on the impact of poor personal values on business operations, with a plan to help the owner improve","Group activity searching the business ethics advocated by the Fair Competition Commission (FCC) and the Zanzibar Fair Competition Commission (ZFCC)"],"resources":["Online/offline sources"],"assessment":["The basic tenets of ethics for small businesses are clearly described"],"periods":"18 (Specific Competence 3.2)"}],[{"topic":"Insurance for Small Businesses","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of business knowledge","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, theories and principles of Business Education","activities":["Explain the basic aspects of insurance for small businesses (meaning, principles, importance, choice of appropriate insurance)"],"methods":["Scenario: a short story about damages in a community, used to identify the risks involved and relate them to insurance"],"resources":["Online/offline sources"],"assessment":["The basic aspects of insurance for small businesses are appropriately explained"],"periods":"40 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"Business Partnerships","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of business knowledge","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the concepts, theories and principles of Business Education","activities":["Describe business partnerships (meaning, types, features, advantages and disadvantages, formation and dissolution)"],"methods":["Role play of the features of running a business as a group, linked to the meaning, features and formation of a partnership","Case study of a partnership business covering formation and dissolution, with discussion of lessons learnt"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and a partnership deed template"],"assessment":["Business partnership is clearly described"],"periods":"40 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic":"Taxes and Levies for Small Businesses in Tanzania","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Describe taxes and levies associated with small businesses in Tanzania (meaning, types, importance and sanctions for non-compliance)"],"methods":["Role play of a busy market with tax/levy payers and collectors, followed by reflection on the meaning and importance of tax","Guest speaker from Local Government and/or the Tanzania Revenue Authority (TRA) or Zanzibar Revenue Authority (ZRA), using prepared guiding questions"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and guidelines from TRA"],"assessment":["Taxes and levies associated with small businesses in Tanzania are clearly described"],"periods":"34 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Communication and Networking for Small Businesses","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of operating a small-scale business","activities":["Describe the basic principles of communication and networking for small businesses"],"methods":["Brainstorm on how friends communicate, linked to the meaning, importance and channels of communication","Scenario comparing a clear and an unclear write-up (business letter or plan) to identify the principles of communication","Brainstorm on networking, then a gallery walk presenting plans for using communication and networking to grow the business club project"],"resources":["Online/offline sources, write-up templates and samples"],"assessment":["The basic principles of communication and networking for small businesses are clearly described"],"periods":"34 (shared across Specific Competence 2.1)"},{"topic":"Pricing Techniques","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of trading locally and internationally","activities":["Use pricing techniques to determine appropriate prices of products"],"methods":["Scenarios on each pricing technique: cost-plus, value, penetration, price skimming, bundle, premium, competitive and psychological pricing","Skills lab: price one product from the group project using the techniques learnt, then present for feedback","Project activity: create a price catalogue for the products"],"resources":["Online/offline sources, price catalogue samples"],"assessment":["Pricing techniques to determine appropriate prices of products are distinctly used"],"periods":"40 (shared across Specific Competence 2.2)"},{"topic":"Buying and Selling Products Within and Outside the Country","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of trading locally and internationally","activities":["Identify relevant procedures and practices for buying and selling products within and outside the country"],"methods":["Scenario of two young people who want to sell to and buy from a neighbouring country but lack the know-how, with students advising them on import and export procedures","Case study on the procedures and practices, with discussion of lessons learnt"],"resources":["Online/offline sources; sample documents for importation and exportation of products"],"assessment":["Relevant procedures and practices for buying and selling products within and outside the country are clearly identified"],"periods":"40 (shared across Specific Competence 2.2)"},{"topic":"Selling Methods and Techniques to Facilitate Trade","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Solve social challenges using business skills","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic skills of trading locally and internationally","activities":["Use appropriate selling methods and techniques (branding, logos, packaging, after-sales services, barcoding, direct mail and internet auctions) to facilitate trade"],"methods":["Brainstorm on students' experiences of buying and selling, linked to selling methods and techniques in preparation for the skills lab"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and samples of products"],"assessment":["Selling methods and techniques to facilitate trade are clearly demonstrated"],"periods":"40 (shared across Specific Competence 2.2)"},{"topic":"Completing and Presenting the Business Plan","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Apply business knowledge in various contexts","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Apply business theories into practice","activities":["Complete and present the business plan developed in Form Three"],"methods":["Group activity: exchange group business plans for peer review and improve them from the feedback","Skills lab: polish and submit the complete business plans, then prepare, rehearse and pitch them in the business club"],"resources":["Online/offline sources and the business plans developed in Form Three"],"assessment":["The business plan is clearly presented"],"periods":"26 (Specific Competence 3.1)"}]]},"Chemistry":{"lang":"en","forms":[[{"topic":"Introduction to Chemistry","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","activities":["Describe the concept of Chemistry (meaning, branches, applications and relationships with other disciplines)","Discuss the contribution of Chemistry in the development of modern society"],"methods":["Brainstorming in groups on the chemical basis of materials and the meaning/importance of Chemistry","Project work exploring common industrial products in Tanzania and relating them to Chemistry","Field visit to a nearby industry, health facility, mining site or farm to appreciate Chemistry's role in society"],"resources":["Pictures, diagrams, simulations, animations or videos illustrating the meaning, branches, applications and relationships of Chemistry"],"assessment":[],"periods":"78 (shared across this Specific Competence)"},{"topic":"Laboratory Techniques and Safety","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Conduct experiments in Chemistry","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Conduct experiments in Chemistry","activities":["Describe basic Chemistry laboratory skills (laboratory rules and precautions, safety measures, first aid, and Chemistry laboratory apparatus)"],"methods":["Group discussion interpreting basic laboratory skills related to rules, precautions, safety measures and chemical warning signs"],"resources":["Laboratory manuals, models, pictures, wall charts with written laboratory rules, first aid kit, laboratory apparatus"],"assessment":[],"periods":"39 (shared with 'Firefighting and Flames', 'Matter' and 'Elements, Compounds and Mixtures')"},{"topic":"Firefighting and Flames","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Conduct experiments in Chemistry","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Conduct experiments in Chemistry","activities":["Describe classes of fire and practise firefighting techniques, as part of basic Chemistry laboratory skills"],"methods":["Guest speaker from the fire brigade to interpret classes of fire and firefighting practice, followed by a written report","Outdoor activity practising extinguishing small fires"],"resources":["Fire extinguishers and videos illustrating basic chemistry laboratory skills","This activity is part of the same 3.1(a) source activity as 'Laboratory Techniques and Safety'."],"assessment":[],"periods":"39 (shared with 'Laboratory Techniques and Safety')"},{"topic":"Matter","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 3.0 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 3.1 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","activities":["Describe the concept of matter (physical and chemical changes of matter)","Perform experiments on the changes of matter from one state to another"],"methods":["Practical work investigating physical/chemical changes of matter using local substances","Experimentation on sublimation, rusting of iron nails, freezing/evaporation of water, and dissolving salts"],"resources":["Ice, water, heat source, evaporating basin, metal nails, beaker, table salt, sugar, iodine crystals, magnet, magnesium ribbon, acids, CuSO4 solution, aluminium foil, candle, CaCO3, Pb(NO3)2 solution and related simulations/videos"],"assessment":[],"periods":"78 (shared, under 1.1) + 39 (shared, under 3.1)"},{"topic":"Elements, Compounds and Mixtures","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 3.0 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 3.1 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","activities":["Describe the concepts of chemical elements (criteria for assigning chemical symbols), compounds (binary compounds) and mixtures (types of solution and separation of mixtures)","Compare the properties of compounds with those of their constituent elements","Perform experiments on separation of different mixtures using different methods"],"methods":["Think-ink-pair-share on industrial products and their constituent elements","Hands-on-minds-on preparation of solutions from home materials","Group discussion and technological-based learning comparing compound and element properties","Experimentation on separation methods (simple/fractional distillation, decantation) with a home-based project on daily-life mixture separation"],"resources":["Periodic table, copper, zinc, aluminium, iron, sulphur, hydrogen, common salt, iron filings, magnet, powdered sulphur, crucible and lid, heat source, HCl solution, water, chalk, FeS, milk, clay soil, margarine, filter paper, funnel, ethanol, iodine crystals, kerosene, ink, sugar, distillation system"],"assessment":[],"periods":"78 (shared, under 1.1) + 39 (shared, under 3.1)"}],[{"topic":"Atomic Structure","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","activities":["Describe the modern concept of atomic structure (Dalton's atomic structure and sub-atomic particles)","Describe the concept of electronic arrangements","Use the concept of atomic structure to determine the atomic and mass numbers of an element"],"methods":["Think-ink-pair-share on the meaning of an atom and its structure, plus ICT-based research and reporting","Technological-based learning (simulations/animations) on electron arrangement, with group model-building using local materials","Group discussion calculating atomic and mass numbers of elements"],"resources":["Diagrams, pictures, wall charts, simulations and videos illustrating Dalton's atomic structure and sub-atomic particles; models/charts showing electronic arrangement, atomic number, protons and neutrons"],"assessment":[],"periods":"81 (shared across this Specific Competence)"},{"topic":"Periodic Classification","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.2","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the physical and chemical properties of elements on the basis of their arrangements in the periodic table","activities":["Explain the changes in the physical and chemical properties of elements across and down the periodic table","Use the electronic configuration of an element to locate its position in the periodic table"],"methods":["Group discussion explaining trends of metallic/non-metallic properties across periods and down groups","Group discussion applying the periodic law to locate elements using electronic configuration"],"resources":["Diagrams, pictures, wall charts, simulations and videos illustrating changes in physical/chemical properties; wall charts of the modern periodic table showing electronic configuration"],"assessment":[],"periods":"18"},{"topic":"Chemical Bonding, Formula and Nomenclature","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","activities":["Explain the concept of chemical formulae and nomenclature (valence, oxidation state, radicals and naming of binary inorganic compounds using the IUPAC system)","Determine empirical and molecular formulae of common compounds","Describe the concept of chemical bonding (covalent and electrovalent bonding)"],"methods":["Inquiry-based learning identifying common names and constituent elements of substances","Group discussion on formula, valence, oxidation state, radicals and IUPAC naming, plus a gallery-work session on formula-writing rules","Group discussion and problem solving determining percentage composition, empirical and molecular formulae","Outdoor activity relating real-world building/bonding to chemical bonding concepts, and technology-based learning using software such as ChemDraw"],"resources":["Valence cards, modern periodic table, wall charts showing oxidation states/common radicals, labelled bottles of laboratory chemicals; models depicting empirical/molecular formulae; selected organic/inorganic structures, computers installed with Chemistry software"],"assessment":[],"periods":"81 (shared across this Specific Competence)"},{"topic":"Chemical Reactions","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","activities":["Describe the concept of chemical reactions (chemical equations, balancing chemical equations, and types of chemical reactions)","Relate the types of chemical reactions with common processes in daily life such as burning of fuel and digestion in living organisms"],"methods":["Group discussion writing simple word and symbol equations","Think-ink-pair-share identifying reaction types and balancing/interpreting equations","Experimentation verifying the law of conservation of matter, with a written report","Project work examining chemical reactions in fuel burning and digestion"],"resources":["Kerosene, candles, KOH/NaOH, HCl, glycerine, selected apparatus and equipment; laboratory note book, heat source and fuel such as charcoal"],"assessment":[],"periods":"81 (shared across this Specific Competence)"},{"topic":"Acids, Bases and Salts","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 2.0 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry / 2.1 Conduct experiments in Chemistry","activities":["Describe acids, bases and salts (reactions of acids and bases with various substances) and their applications in daily life","Prepare acid-base indicators using locally available materials","Use the prepared indicators to test acidity and alkalinity of substances found in the locality"],"methods":["Inquiry-based learning analysing acidic/basic substances from the environment","Group discussion describing reactions of acids and bases, plus field trips to food/beverage processing industries","Outdoor activity preparing indicators from coloured flowers/leaves","Experimentation testing acidity/alkalinity using the prepared indicators"],"resources":["Citrus fruits, vinegar, sour milk, apples, wood ash, toothpaste, baking powder, mineral acids, hydroxides and indicators; coloured flowers/leaves, mortar and pestle, lemon/tomato juice, soft drinks, NaOH"],"assessment":[],"periods":"81 (shared, under 1.1) + 18 (shared, under 2.1)"}],[{"topic":"Chemical Equations","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate mastery of concepts, theories and principles in Chemistry","activities":["In the syllabus document received, chemical equations (word/symbol equations, balancing, and types of chemical reactions) are detailed under Form Two (the same source material used for the Form Two 'Chemical Reactions' topic above), not under Form Three. No additional or more advanced Form Three treatment of chemical equations appears in this document. Presented here under the Form Three heading as given, with this placement flagged for verification."],"methods":["In the syllabus document received, chemical equations (word/symbol equations, balancing, and types of chemical reactions) are detailed under Form Two (the same source material used for the Form Two 'Chemical Reactions' topic above), not under Form Three. No additional or more advanced Form Three treatment of chemical equations appears in this document. Presented here under the Form Three heading as given, with this placement flagged for verification."],"resources":["In the syllabus document received, chemical equations (word/symbol equations, balancing, and types of chemical reactions) are detailed under Form Two (the same source material used for the Form Two 'Chemical Reactions' topic above), not under Form Three. No additional or more advanced Form Three treatment of chemical equations appears in thi