stances using qualitative analysis procedures","Group discussion describing behaviours/properties of cations and anions in chemical reactions"],"resources":["Qualitative analysis reagents, apparatus for qualitative analysis, qualitative analysis sheets, wall charts and samples of salts"],"assessment":[],"periods":"36 (shared across the two related activities in this competence group)"}]]},"Computer Application":{"lang":"en","forms":[[{"topic":"Familiarizing Yourself with a Computer","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Introduction to computer","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Organising a microcomputer and its peripherals","activities":["Familiarize yourself with a computer (computer hardware and software, parts and their functions)"],"methods":["Demonstration: show students different parts of the computer and assist them to familiarise with its parts and functions","Questions and Answers: explain the concepts of the computer system and describe computer hardware and software","Hands-on activities: practise identification of computer systems and how they work by starting and shutting down a computer"],"resources":["Computer; computer peripherals (USB, HDMI, VGA, DVI, ethernet cable); overhead projector; internet access"],"assessment":["Demonstrate basic knowledge of a computer"],"periods":"12 (shared across Unit 1.1)"},{"topic":"Connecting Peripherals to a Micro-computer","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Introduction to computer","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Organising a microcomputer and its peripherals","activities":["Connect peripherals to a micro-computer"],"methods":["Brainstorming on peripheral devices for a micro-computer","Demonstration: show how to connect peripherals to a micro-computer","Questions and Answers: elaborate the procedures for connecting peripherals to the micro-computer system","Hands-on activity: practise connecting and disconnecting peripherals"],"resources":["Computer peripherals (USB, HDMI, VGA, DVI, ethernet cable); computer; overhead projector; internet access"],"assessment":["Ability to properly connect peripherals to a micro-computer"],"periods":"12 (shared across Unit 1.1)"},{"topic":"Connecting a Computer to the Internet","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Introduction to computer","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Organising a microcomputer and its peripherals","activities":["Connect a computer to the internet"],"methods":["Think Ink Pair Share on the concept of network","Group discussion in manageable groups on the concept of internet","Demonstration: show how to connect the computer to the internet using wired or wireless connection","Hands-on activities: connect computers to the internet and search for material or topics"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; material to be searched from internet; ethernet cables"],"assessment":["Ability to successfully connect the computer to the internet"],"periods":"12 (shared across Unit 1.1)"},{"topic":"Introduction to Word Processing","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Word Processing","activities":["Introduction to word processing (concepts of a word processor)"],"methods":["Group discussion in reasonably sized groups on the concepts of a word processor"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; MS Word program"],"assessment":["Exhibit introductory knowledge in word processing"],"periods":"12 (shared across Unit 2.1)"},{"topic":"Working with Microsoft Office Word","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Word Processing","activities":["Work with Microsoft Office Word: create and save documents, and format documents (page numbers, text attributes, page layout, tables and pictures)"],"methods":["Demonstration: show how to create a document using the word processor and how to format it by inserting page numbers, text attributes, page layout, tables and pictures","Questions and Answers: explain different types of toolbars and their functions","Practical Activity: create and save a word document; practise inserting numbering, bullets, page numbers, header, footer and text attributes; practise inserting and formatting tables and pictures"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; Microsoft Word program"],"assessment":["Ability to work with Microsoft Office Word"],"periods":"12 (shared across Unit 2.1)"}],[{"topic":"Spreadsheet Creation, Formatting, Data Entry, Organization, Sort and Filter","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Working with spreadsheets","activities":["Perform spreadsheet creation, formatting, data entry, organization, sorting and filtering"],"methods":["Demonstration: show step by step how to use various tools and properties available in the spreadsheet and how to perform data entry, sorting and filtering; guide on adding tables, formatting tables and sorting data in tables","Hands-on activities: give students a set of data and task them to insert it in Excel, sort it and filter it"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; Excel program"],"assessment":["Ability to work with spreadsheet applications"],"periods":"34 (shared across Unit 2.2)"},{"topic":"Basic Calculations and Formulas","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Working with spreadsheets","activities":["Perform basic calculations and formulas"],"methods":["Demonstration: show the correct use of arithmetic operators (addition, subtraction, multiplication and division) in basic formulas","Practical Activity: in small groups, perform assigned calculations on a set of data in a spreadsheet","Project Activity: manage a budget using a spreadsheet, apply percentage increases and create summaries using SUM, AVERAGE and percentage formulas"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; MS Excel program"],"assessment":["Ability to perform basic calculations and formulas"],"periods":"34 (shared across Unit 2.2)"},{"topic":"Data Validation and Conditional Formatting","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Working with spreadsheets","activities":["Perform data validation and conditional formatting"],"methods":["Demonstration: show features of data validation and conditional formatting","Practical Activity: provide data that must be validated and conditionally formatted, then let students perform the task","Project-Based Activity: apply data validation and conditional formatting in real-world scenarios","Group Discussion: collaborative activities, quizzes and interactive tasks to reinforce learning"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; MS Excel program"],"assessment":["Ability to perform data validation and conditional formatting"],"periods":"34 (shared across Unit 2.2)"},{"topic":"Data Import and Export","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Working with spreadsheets","activities":["Perform data import and export"],"methods":["Demonstration: use a projector or screen-sharing software to show the step-by-step process of importing data from different sources (e.g., CSV files, databases) and exporting to various formats","Practical Activity: provide sample files to import into spreadsheets and exercises requiring export in various formats; develop worksheets outlining the steps with screenshots and tips","Project-Based Activity: collect data from various sources, import it into a spreadsheet, then export reports or presentations"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; MS Excel program; CSV files; internet access"],"assessment":["Capability to perform data import and export correctly"],"periods":"34 (shared across Unit 2.2)"},{"topic":"Page Setup and Printing","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.2","sc":"Working with spreadsheets","activities":["Perform page setup and printing"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate page layout setup and printing processes; provide spreadsheet samples with various formatting requirements for students to adjust and print; create step-by-step guides or checklists","Group Discussion: group activities where students collaborate on page layout tasks"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; MS Excel program; printer"],"assessment":["Ability to perform page setup and printing correctly"],"periods":"34 (shared across Unit 2.2)"},{"topic":"Familiarizing with a Database Application","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.3","sc":"Working with database applications","activities":["Familiarize with a database application (concept of database, common vendors, opening and closing database software)"],"methods":["Group Discussion: discuss the concept of database using real-life examples and explain common vendors of database applications","Demonstration: show various tools and properties available in the database software and how to open and close it","Hands-on activities: use the internet to watch tutorials on creating a database using Microsoft Access and explain its advantages and features"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; database program; internet access; Access overview tutorials"],"assessment":["Ability to work correctly with database applications"],"periods":"26 (shared across Unit 2.3 Database)"},{"topic":"Creating Tables and Entering Data","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.3","sc":"Working with database applications","activities":["Create tables and enter data"],"methods":["Demonstration: use video to show how database forms are created; use a real-world database such as examination results to show how tables are created","Practical: create tables and enter data using real-world scenarios","Project-based activities: assign a scenario where students create a table of several data items"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; database program; internet access; Access overview tutorials"],"assessment":["Ability to create tables and enter data correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across Unit 2.3 Database)"},{"topic":"Creating Queries","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.3","sc":"Working with database applications","activities":["Create queries"],"methods":["Demonstration: show how to create queries","Practical: guide students on how to create queries","Project-based activities: assign a scenario where students create queries from several data items"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; database program; internet access; data for query creation"],"assessment":["Ability to create queries correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across Unit 2.3 Database)"},{"topic":"Creating Forms","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.3","sc":"Working with database applications","activities":["Create forms"],"methods":["Demonstration: use guided video tutorials to show how database forms are created; use a real-world database to show how tables are created","Practical: guide students on creating forms and entering data"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; database program; internet access; data for form creation"],"assessment":["Ability to create forms and tables with several data items correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across Unit 2.3 Database)"},{"topic":"Creating Reports","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.3","sc":"Working with database applications","activities":["Create reports"],"methods":["Demonstration: use guided video tutorials to show how database reports are created; use a real-world database to show how reports are created","Practical: create reports and assign the data to be used","Project-based activities: assign a scenario where students create a report from several data items"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; database program; internet access; data for report creation"],"assessment":["Ability to create data reports correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across Unit 2.3 Database)"},{"topic":"Creating, Formatting Presentations and Organizing Slide Content","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.4","sc":"Working with presentation applications","activities":["Create and format presentations and organize slide content"],"methods":["Demonstration: use a projector or screen-sharing to show how to navigate the presentation software, including creating slides, adding content and formatting options","Practical Activity: hands-on workshops practising creating presentations; develop printed or digital handouts outlining the process of creating and formatting slides","Group Discussion: in manageable groups, create a presentation on a specific topic using PowerPoint"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; presentation program; internet access; presentation creation handout","Note: the source table labels this unit '2.3 Working with presentation applications', duplicating the number used for database applications. Table 1 of the same syllabus numbers it 2.4; that numbering is used here."],"assessment":["Ability to work with presentation applications correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across the presentation unit)"},{"topic":"Inserting Images, Graphics and SmartArt","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.4","sc":"Working with presentation applications","activities":["Insert images, graphics and SmartArt"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate inserting and formatting images, graphics and SmartArt","Hands-on activities: practise inserting and manipulating visual elements; workshops focused on designing effective visual presentations","Case study: present real-world examples of well-designed presentations"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; presentation program; internet access; presentation creation handout"],"assessment":["Ability to insert images, graphics and SmartArt accurately"],"periods":"26 (shared across the presentation unit)"},{"topic":"Incorporating Charts and Tables","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.4","sc":"Working with presentation applications","activities":["Incorporate charts and tables"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate how to create, insert and format charts and tables in presentation software (e.g., Microsoft PowerPoint, Google Slides)","Practical Activity: practise creating charts and tables with real or sample data; organise workshops focused on creating visually effective charts and tables"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; presentation program; internet access; presentation creation handout"],"assessment":["Ability to incorporate charts and tables correctly"],"periods":"26 (shared across the presentation unit)"},{"topic":"Creating Slide Transitions, Slide Master and Animations","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.4","sc":"Working with presentation applications","activities":["Create slide transitions, apply a slide master and add animations"],"methods":["Demonstration: show how to create slide transitions, apply a Slide Master and add animations"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; presentation program; internet access"],"assessment":["Ability to create transitions between slides, use slide master layouts and ensure uniformity across slides"],"periods":"26 (shared across the presentation unit)"},{"topic":"Creating Presentations for Remote Meetings","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.4","sc":"Working with presentation applications","activities":["Create presentations for remote meetings"],"methods":["Demonstration: show how to create a presentation tailored for remote delivery, emphasising clarity, simplicity and engaging design","Practical Activity: hands-on activity using remote meeting platforms (e.g., Zoom, Google Meet, Microsoft Teams) to share presentations","Group Discussion: collaborative group work to design a remote presentation"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; presentation program; internet access; presentation creation handout"],"assessment":["Presentations for remote meetings are appropriately performed"],"periods":"26 (shared across the presentation unit)"}],[{"topic":"Document Creation and Formatting (Desktop Publishing)","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.5","sc":"Working with desktop publishing","activities":["Perform document creation and formatting in desktop publishing software"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate the basic features of MS Publisher, such as selecting templates, customizing layouts, inserting images and formatting text","Project-Based Activity: provide structured, step-by-step instructions to create and format a document in MS Publisher","Project-Based Activity: create a complete publication from scratch based on a real-world scenario"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; Publisher program; internet access; Publisher creation handout","Note: the source table labels this unit '2.4 Working with desktop publishing'; Table 1 of the same syllabus numbers it 2.5, which is used here."],"assessment":["Ability to create documents and format them accurately"],"periods":"31 (shared across the desktop publishing unit)"},{"topic":"Image Insertion, Editing and Use of Graphics and Design Elements","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.5","sc":"Working with desktop publishing","activities":["Perform image insertion, editing and use of graphics and design elements"],"methods":["Demonstration: conduct a demonstration of inserting images and graphics into a publication, showing how to use different editing tools in MS Publisher","Practical Activity: facilitate hands-on practice sessions where students follow along and apply what they learned in real time"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; Publisher program; internet access"],"assessment":["Ability to perform image insertion, editing and use graphics and design elements correctly"],"periods":"31 (shared across the desktop publishing unit)"},{"topic":"Typography and Font Management","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.5","sc":"Working with desktop publishing","activities":["Perform typography and font management"],"methods":["Demonstration: provide live demonstrations of how to access and manage fonts in desktop publishing software","Project-Based Activity: hands-on projects applying typography principles in creating documents or publications","Think Ink Pair Share: group workshops where students present their work for peer critique, focusing on typography choices","Research-Based Activity: research a typography resource (e.g., Google Fonts, Adobe Fonts) and present findings to the class"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; Publisher program; internet access; Publisher creation handout"],"assessment":["Ability to perform typography and font management precisely"],"periods":"31 (shared across the desktop publishing unit)"},{"topic":"Designing Office and Business Products","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Office application","scCode":"2.5","sc":"Working with desktop publishing","activities":["Design office and business products (business cards, stationery, brochures, flyers, posters, newsletters, invitations and greeting cards)"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate how to prepare business cards and stationery","Practical Activity: create brochures and flyers, make posters, design newsletters, create invitations and greeting cards"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; Publisher program; internet access"],"assessment":["Applicability of office and business products suitably"],"periods":"31 (shared across the desktop publishing unit)"},{"topic":"Conducting Internet Search","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Conduct internet search (web browsers, search engines, search techniques, credible and reliable sources)"],"methods":["Brainstorming on the internet and its terminologies","Group Discussion: explain different web browsers, search engines and their functionalities; describe different internet search techniques; identify credible and reliable sources of information","Practical Activity: use the internet for searching information"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; web browser application"],"assessment":["Precision use of internet search"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Working with Email Applications","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Work with email applications (set up accounts, compose/send/reply, organise with folders and labels, attach files, manage the inbox)"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: describe concepts of email applications and their terminologies","Practical Activity: set up an email account and configure settings (signatures, automatic replies); compose, send and reply to emails professionally; use folders and labels to organise emails; attach files, images and documents securely","Practical Activity: use email tools such as filters, rules and priority markers to manage the inbox efficiently"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; email applications"],"assessment":["Ability to perform email application tasks appropriately"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Administering Social Media Accounts","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Administer social media accounts (creating and posting content, managing multiple accounts, responding to interactions, reading analytics)"],"methods":["Brainstorming on different types of social media accounts and their applications","Case Study: use real-world scenarios to illustrate creating and posting content, emphasising differences in tone and style across platforms; analyse social media interactions and develop response strategies (customer inquiries, complaints, engagement)","Practical Activity: practise using social media management tools to schedule posts and manage multiple accounts; set up various social media accounts","Demonstration: demonstrate how to read and interpret social media analytics to measure performance and make improvements"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; social media applications"],"assessment":["Ability to administer and exhibit awareness about social media accounts"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Administering Webinars and Virtual Meetings","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Administer webinars and virtual meetings"],"methods":["Demonstration: demonstrate various virtual meeting platforms and guide students in setting up meetings or webinars, focusing on essential tools and settings","Practical Activity: schedule meetings, create invitations, and use features like screen sharing, breakout rooms and polls","Group Discussion: in manageable groups, describe different types of webinars or virtual meetings"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; webinar application subscriptions"],"assessment":["Ability to set meetings or webinars using essential tools"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Creating Online Forms and Surveys","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Create online forms and surveys"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: describe different types of online forms and their applications","Practical Activity: guide students through the process of selecting a platform and creating an online form or survey"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access"],"assessment":["Ability to create online forms and surveys correctly"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Working with Cloud Storage and File Sharing","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Administering internet applications","activities":["Work with cloud storage and file sharing"],"methods":["Think Ink Pair Share: think individually about cloud storage and its terminologies, then share with the class","Practical Activity: create and set up cloud storage accounts on different platforms; upload, organise and share files with various permission levels to understand file security and accessibility; practise using cloud services across multiple devices, ensuring files sync properly and troubleshooting common issues"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access"],"assessment":["Ability to work with cloud storage and file sharing properly"],"periods":"31 (shared across Unit 3.1)"},{"topic":"Recognising Internet Threats","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.2","sc":"Administering internet safety","activities":["Recognise internet threats and their potential consequences"],"methods":["Case Study: use case studies to explain various types of internet threats and their potential consequences, with real-life examples of cyber-attacks","Group Discussion: lead discussions on how cybercriminals use social engineering to manipulate users, encouraging students to share personal experiences or examples encountered"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; cyber-crime act summary","Note: in the Form Three detailed table this element is listed under Unit 3.1; it is mapped here to Unit 3.2 'Administering internet safety' from Table 1, which is the unit its content corresponds to."],"assessment":["Ability to identify and recognize internet threats"],"periods":"31 (listed under Unit 3.1 in the source table)"},{"topic":"Using Virtual Private Network (VPN) and Proxy","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.2","sc":"Administering internet safety","activities":["Use a virtual private network (VPN) and proxy"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: explain the concepts of VPNs and proxies, highlighting their differences and typical use cases","Practical Activity: install, configure and use VPN software or proxy settings on different devices, ensuring students understand how to select VPN servers and manage encryption settings"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; VPN software","As above, this element is listed under Unit 3.1 in the source table but corresponds to Unit 3.2 'Administering internet safety' in Table 1."],"assessment":["Ability to use a virtual private network (VPN) and proxy correctly"],"periods":"31 (listed under Unit 3.1 in the source table)"}],[{"topic":"Creating Email Marketing","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Create email marketing (templates, segmented lists, personalization and automated campaigns)"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: introduce the basics of email marketing, explaining how it integrates with overall marketing strategies and customer engagement","Practical Activity: design email templates using different email marketing platforms, focusing on design, messaging and call-to-action buttons; create a segmented email list and explain the importance of personalization and targeting","Demonstration: demonstrate how to set up automated email campaigns such as welcome emails, promotional campaigns or follow-up emails using autoresponders"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; email software"],"assessment":["Ability to create email marketing correctly"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Creating Digital Contents","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Create digital contents (social media posts, blog articles, video snippets) and apply content strategies ethically and legally"],"methods":["Brainstorming on the different types of digital content, with examples of how businesses and influencers use them for brand building, engagement and marketing","Practical Activity: create various types of content using relevant tools to develop polished, engaging work; craft content strategies for different platforms focusing on audience engagement, tone and branding","Cover copyright laws, creative commons licensing and ethical considerations when using third-party assets"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; video editing software; cyber-crime act"],"assessment":["Ability to create digital contents"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Customizing Blogs for Publication","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Customize blogs for publication"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: introduce blog platforms and provide demonstrations of setting up and customizing blogs with different themes and designs","Practical Activity: customize the appearance and structure of their blogs, ensuring they reflect the desired look and purpose"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; blog and website platforms"],"assessment":["Competency in customization of blogs for publications"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Conducting Online Advertising","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Conduct online advertising (ad copy and visuals, audience targeting, budgets and bidding, campaign optimisation)"],"methods":["Question and Answer: introduce the basics of online advertising, explaining the different types of ads and how they fit into broader digital marketing strategies","Demonstration: demonstrate how to craft effective ad copy and visuals, explaining how design choices influence ad performance; exercises selecting and adjusting targeting options; explain how to set budgets and use bidding strategies and monitor campaign performance using key metrics","Practical Activity: analyse campaign data and make real-time adjustments to improve performance, optimising ads based on impressions, clicks and conversion rates"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; video editing software; social media software"],"assessment":["Ability to conduct online advertising correctly"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Conducting Market Analytics and Reporting","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Conduct market analytics and reporting"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: explain the importance of market analytics and how it supports strategic decision-making, with real-world examples of its impact","Practical Activity: work with tools like Google Analytics, Excel or other platforms to gather and interpret market data for websites and online campaigns","Demonstration: demonstrate how to track and analyse key metrics such as traffic, conversion rates and user demographics; group exercises identifying market trends and customer behaviour patterns; create professional reports with clear visualizations","Case Study: apply analytical findings to real-life business scenarios and make strategic recommendations based on the data"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; social media software"],"assessment":["Ability to make market analytics and reporting accurately"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Maintaining Customer Relationship (CRM) Systems","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Maintain customer relationship management (CRM) systems, including data protection compliance"],"methods":["Questions and Answers: clarify the purpose and benefits of CRM systems, with examples of how businesses use them to manage relationships and drive sales","Practical Activity: set up a CRM system, configure its features and manage customer data; practise automating common tasks such as sending follow-up emails or updating customer records after interactions","Demonstration: demonstrate how to use CRM tools for tracking leads, sales activities and customer interactions; cover regulations like GDPR or CCPA to ensure customer data is protected"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; social media software; customer relationship management system"],"assessment":["Ability to maintain customer relationship (CRM) systems effectively"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"},{"topic":"Working with Artificial Intelligence (AI)","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Implementing internet and digital marketing","scCode":"3.3","sc":"Administering digital marketing","activities":["Work with artificial intelligence (AI) tools"],"methods":["Brainstorming on artificial intelligence and its terminologies","Group Discussion: in groups, explain different artificial intelligence tools and their functionalities; describe different techniques for using AI tools; identify credible AI tools and how to purchase them","Practical Activity: use AI to search, analyse, develop images and solve subject questions"],"resources":["Computer; overhead projector; internet access; AI tools subscription"],"assessment":["Ability to use artificial intelligence (AI)"],"periods":"42 (shared across Unit 3.3)"}]]},"Computer Science":{"lang":"en","forms":[[{"topic":"Concept of Computer Science","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the basic concepts of Computer Science","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Understand the field of Computer Science and its related fields","activities":["Describe the concept of Computer Science (meaning, importance, application)"],"methods":["Brainstorming and Think-Ink-Pair-Share (TIPS) to describe the concept of Computer Science"],"resources":["Handouts with contents of Computer Science concepts"],"assessment":["Confidently describe the concept of the Computer Science field"],"periods":"8 (shared across Specific Competence 1.1)"},{"topic"