ies":["Express opinions through debates, dialogues and impromptu speeches using formulaic language (e.g., In my opinion…, I would say…)","Present facts logically using appropriate formulaic language"],"methods":["Debate using formulaic language to give opinions","Dialogue reading/acting on opinion topics","Guided delivery of impromptu speeches on opinion topics","Presentation and debate practice presenting facts formulaically"],"resources":["Speakers, recorded materials (audio/video clips, recorded stories) on various situations","Periods shared with 'Participating in an Interview' and other 4.1 activities — 16 in total"],"assessment":[],"periods":"16 (shared with 'Participating in an Interview')"},{"topic":"Formal Letter and Email Writing","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Comprehend oral and written information","scCode":"3.2","sc":"Create a variety of texts for different communicative purposes using the appropriate tone and register","activities":["Write claim and request letters in different contexts (e.g., learning facilities, sports gear, result reports)","Compose e-mails on various issues using appropriate language"],"methods":["Discussion of considerations for official letters, then guided letter-writing practice","Gallery walk on email components/considerations, then guided composing of emails on various issues"],"resources":["Relevant texts, dictionaries, samples of claim and request letters","Note: in the syllabus document received, this content (claim/request letters and emails) is placed under Form Two, not Form Three. Presented here under the Form Three heading as given, with this placement flagged for verification."],"assessment":[],"periods":"21 (shared with 'Create short stories on various topics', also part of the same Form Two competence)"}],[{"topic":"Expressing Oneself","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of English language skills","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Use appropriate grammar and vocabulary in oral and in written language tasks","activities":["Prepare 