ng content is placed under Form One (Specific Competence 4.2), not Form Four. Presented here under the Form Four heading as given, with this placement flagged for verification."],"assessment":[],"periods":"18"},{"topic":"Reading Literary Work","mcCode":"5.0","mc":"Appreciate and create literary works","scCode":"5.1","sc":"Appreciate the aesthetics and value of literature","activities":["Assess the language used in a selected novella","Compare own values and perspectives with those implied in a selected novella","Dramatise episodes from a selected novella"],"methods":["Brainstorming techniques for analysing language, then close reading to assess language used in the novella","TIPS technique and pair work comparing own values/perspectives with the novella's","Group dramatisation of episodes from the novella"],"resources":["A variety of literary texts, dictionaries"],"assessment":[],"periods":"10"},{"topic":"Speaking using Appropriate Language, Content and Style","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Communicate effectively in different contexts","scCode":"3.1","sc":"Use appropriate grammar and vocabulary for oral communication in a variety of contexts","activities":["Express feelings depicted/portrayed in various social contexts using appropriate phrases (e.g., I am saddened…, I feel happy…)","Deliver different kinds of planned and unplanned speeches (e.g., informative, persuasive) on different topics","Negotiate solutions to various problems using appropriate formulaic language"],"methods":["Pictures, case study/scenario and dialogue to practise expressing feelings appropriately","Discussion of speech types followed by guided delivery of planned/unplanned speeches","Roleplay and dialogue negotiating solutions using formulaic language"],"resources":["Dictionaries, relevant texts (e.g., books for English grammar)"],"assessment":[],"periods":"11"},{"topic":"Writing Application Letters","mcCode":"3.0","mc":"Communicate effectively in different contexts","scCode":"3.2","sc":"Create a variety of texts for different communicative purposes using the appropriate tone and register","activities":["Write application letters for various purposes (e.g., job application, school admission)"],"methods":["Information search on the types and parts of application letters","Pair work writing application letters for various purposes"],"resources":["Dictionaries, encyclopaedia, relevant texts","Periods shared with 'Write speeches on a variety of topics' and 'Write Curriculum Vitae (CV)' under the same Specific Competence — 14 in total"],"assessment":[],"periods":"14 (shared with related writing activities in the same competence)"}]]},"Geography":{"lang":"en","forms":[[{"topic":"Introduction to Geography","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the origin and the structure of the Earth and Earth systems","activities":["Explain the concept and scope of Geography (branches, importance and relationship with other disciplines)"],"methods":["Brainstorming: meaning, branches and importance of Geography, and its relationship with other disciplines","Field Observation: observe landforms, vegetation and human activities to support the concept of Geography and summarise their importance in relation to other disciplines"],"resources":["Relevant books, charts, and ICT simulation tools on the concept of Geography"],"assessment":[],"periods":"9"},{"topic":"The Planet Earth","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the origin and the structure of the Earth and Earth systems","activities":["Describe the Earth: origin, shape, size and position of the Earth in the solar system"],"methods":["Brainstorming: origin, shape, size and position of the Earth in the solar system","Field Observation: observe the Earth's surface and identify components of the solar system","Project work: design a model of the components of the solar system (size, shape, distance, position) and present in class"],"resources":["Relevant books, globe, picture of the solar system, relevant ICT simulation tools and models on the planet Earth","Periods shared with 'Movements of the Earth in the Solar System' (80 in total)"],"assessment":[],"periods":"80 (shared with the next topic)"},{"topic":"Movements of the Earth in the Solar System","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the origin and the structure of the Earth and Earth systems","activities":["Describe the movements of the Earth in the solar system, and parallels and meridians"],"methods":["Brainstorming: movements of the Earth in the solar system, and parallels and meridians","Field Observation: observe the Earth's surface and identify components of the solar system","Project work: design a model of the components of the solar system and present in class"],"resources":["Relevant books, globe, picture of the solar system, relevant ICT simulation tools and models on the planet Earth"],"assessment":[],"periods":"80 (shared with the previous topic)"},{"topic":"Major Features of the Earth's Surface","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.2","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the major features of the Earth surface","activities":["Describe major features of the Earth's surface: continents, oceans, major relief features and large inland water bodies"],"methods":["Questions & Answers: mention landforms available in their surroundings","Field observation: visit nearby landforms and water bodies to examine formation, distribution and importance to communities","Group Discussion: discuss the size and distribution of continents, then present in class"],"resources":["Environment, relevant books, relief maps, globe/models, and relevant ICT simulation tools","Periods shared with 'Vegetation' (76 in total)"],"assessment":[],"periods":"76 (shared with the next topic)"},{"topic":"Vegetation","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.2","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the major features of the Earth surface","activities":["Describe the major vegetation zones of the Earth's surface"],"methods":["Field observation: visit nearby vegetation available in their communities to examine distribution and importance to communities","Group Discussion: discuss the distribution of world vegetation zones, then present in class"],"resources":["Environment, relevant books, relief maps, globe/models, and relevant ICT simulation tools"],"assessment":[],"periods":"76 (shared with the previous topic)"}],[{"topic":"The Internal Structure of the Earth","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the origin and the structure of the Earth and Earth systems","activities":["Describe the internal structure of the Earth (crust, mantle, core) and their major characteristics (location, size/thickness, density and gross composition)"],"methods":["Brainstorming: internal structure of the Earth","Group work: design models and drawings to characterise the internal structure of the Earth"],"resources":["Relevant books, globe/models, environment, and flash cards with content on internal structure of the Earth"],"assessment":[],"periods":"27"},{"topic":"The External Structure of the Earth","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the origin and the structure of the Earth and Earth systems","activities":["Describe the main external Earth systems (Hydrosphere, Atmosphere and Biosphere)"],"methods":["Questions & Answers: explain the main external Earth systems","Field observation: observe and discuss the hydrosphere, atmosphere and biosphere with cases from their communities","Independent library study: examine the main external Earth systems"],"resources":["Relevant books, globe/models, environment, relevant ICT tools, flash cards with content on external structure of the Earth (atmosphere, hydrosphere, biosphere and cryosphere)"],"assessment":[],"periods":"24"},{"topic":"Map Reading and Interpretation","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic skills and techniques in Geography","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the basic techniques of map and photograph interpretation","activities":["Describe the basic principles of reading and interpreting maps (key, symbols, direction, margin/frame, map title, scale and contour patterns)","Read and interpret various types of maps and their importance (topographical and statistical maps)"],"methods":["Brainstorming: basic principles of reading and interpreting maps","Group Discussion: discuss basic principles of reading and interpreting maps","Case Study: interpret and analyse various types of maps and their importance to the community"],"resources":["Maps, relevant books, and relevant ICT simulation tools"],"assessment":[],"periods":"32"},{"topic":"Photograph Reading and Interpretation","mcCode":"2.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of basic skills and techniques in Geography","scCode":"2.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the basic techniques of map and photograph interpretation","activities":["Describe the basic concept of photograph in Geography (meaning, types, elements and uses)","Describe the basic principles of photograph interpretation (identifying foreground, middle ground and background, associating objects with geographical phenomena)"],"methods":["Brainstorming: meaning, types, elements and importance of photographs in Geography","Group Discussion: basic uses of photographs / identifying parts of photographs and associating with geographical phenomena","Guest Speaker: cartographer/photographer to share experience on uses of photographs","Question & Answers and Case Study: interpret different cases of geographical phenomena using photographs"],"resources":["Relevant books and photographs (ground, vertical and oblique), magazines/newspapers, camera, and relevant ICT tools"],"assessment":[],"periods":"53 (27 + 26)"}],[{"topic":"The Structure of the Earth","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.1","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the relationship between relief, climate and natural vegetation","activities":["Describe the relationship between major features of the Earth's surface, climate, and natural vegetation"],"methods":["Question & Answers: describe the relationship between major features of the Earth's surface, climate and natural vegetation","Case study: justify the relationship between major features of the Earth's surface, climate and natural vegetation"],"resources":["Maps, photographs, globe and online materials on the relationship between major features of the Earth's surface, climate and natural vegetation","Note: the crust/mantle/core sense of 'structure of the Earth' was already covered in Form II under Main Competence 1.0; the Form III content available under this heading concerns the surface–climate–vegetation relationship, not internal structure."],"assessment":[],"periods":"24"},{"topic":"Forces that Affect the Earth","mcCode":"1.0","mc":"Demonstrate mastery of the structure of the Earth","scCode":"1.2","sc":"Demonstrate an understanding of the major features of the Earth surface","activities":["Placed here because internal Earth-forming forces (folding, faulting, volcanicity, earthquakes) explain how major relief features arise, which falls under Specific Competence 1.2. However, the specific Learning Activities, Methods, Assessment Criteria and Resources for this topic are not present in the Geography syllabus document received — the uploaded Form Three table only details Specific Competences 1.1 (relief–climate–vegetation relationship), 2.1 (land surveying) and the start of 3.1 (research project). Please share the f